 "equipment_type": "Laboratory VAV controller (fume hood)",
 "applies_to": "Variable air volume fume hoods with one or two vertical sashes and a Venturi air valve on the exhaust, run by the Siemens BACnet programmable fume hood controller with sash sensors and an operator display panel.",
 "summary": "Application 6742 runs a VAV fume hood with vertical sashes and a Venturi exhaust air valve on a Siemens BACnet programmable fume hood controller over BACnet MS/TP. It calculates the open sash area, sets the exhaust airflow setpoint to hold the face velocity setpoint, and drives the valve with a 0-10 V signal (EXH AO3) using a calibrated valve table. Occupied and unoccupied face velocity setpoints, sash alerts, flow warnings and alarms, and an emergency purge mode are built in.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "AI and BI objects are read-only. AO and BO objects are BACnet output objects with a priority array; the guide has no access column, so access is inferred from object type. Many AOs are calculated status values, not commands.",
  "Instances shown in braces in the guide may be unbundled at a field panel; that marking is not reproduced here.",
  "Units are given in US units (cfm, fpm, ft², in, inH2O); the guide also lists SI factory defaults.",
  "The same guide (140-1344) also covers application 6741 (damper); that table is a separate entry.",
  "The Venturi valve is calibrated with CAL EXH VLV (BO 78); EXH VLV STAT (BO 79) shows the result. TABLE VOLTS / TABLE FLOW / V TABLE PT (AO 118-120) view and edit the valve table.",
  "STARTUP MODE (AO 21): 0 = normal, 1 and 2 = decommission modes, 3 = start-up with alarms off (factory default).",
  "The point database for application 6742 is on pages 35-38 of the guide."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "BACnet Programmable Fume Hood Controller Vertical Sash Configuration with Damper or Venturi Valve, Application 6741 and Application 6742, Application Note",
  "doc_number": "140-1344",
  "revision_date": "2015-11-09",
  "url": "https://sid.siemens.com/api/khub/documents/jZXTMijdgHr2UijYRScCYw/content"
 },
 "integration": {
  "summary": "Address the controller on the BACnet MS/TP trunk (manually or with auto addressing), calibrate the Venturi valve and set STARTUP MODE to normal. The BMS can set occupancy with OCC.UNOCC (BO 20) and the face velocity setpoints, and reads face velocity, exhaust airflow, sash area and the alarm points.",
  "minimum_points": [
   {
    "ref": "BO 20",
    "name": "OCC.UNOCC",
    "why": "OCC = occupied face velocity setpoint in use"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AO 84",
    "name": "OCC FV STPT",
    "why": "Occupied face velocity setpoint, fpm"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AO 85",
    "name": "UNOC FV STPT",
    "why": "Unoccupied face velocity setpoint, fpm"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AO 4",
    "name": "FACE VEL",
    "why": "Calculated face velocity, fpm"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AI 31",
    "name": "EXH VOL",
    "why": "Measured hood exhaust airflow, cfm"
   },
   {
    "ref": "AO 54",
    "name": "FACE AREA",
    "why": "Sash open area, ft²"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BO 5",
    "name": "LOW ALM",
    "why": "Low flow alarm"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BO 6",
    "name": "HIGH ALM",
    "why": "High flow alarm"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BO 7",
    "name": "EMER ALM",
    "why": "Emergency purge alarm"
   },
   {
    "ref": "BO 8",
    "name": "GEN FAILURE",
    "why": "General failure (sensor or hardware)"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "No enable point: the controller runs its sequence once STARTUP MODE (AO 21) is 0. OCC.UNOCC (BO 20) picks the occupied or unoccupied face velocity setpoint; the guide drives it from DI 2.",
  "heartbeat": null,
  "remote_sensors": null,
  "setup": [
   "BACnet MS/TP only. CTLR ADDRESS (AO 1) holds the MS/TP address; the point table lists its factory value as 99.",
   "APPLICATION (AO 2) holds the application number; the point table lists its factory default as 6700."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "STARTUP MODE (AO 21) ships at 3 (start-up: control works but alarms are off and the display shows Startup). Set it to 0 for normal operation; 1 and 2 are decommission modes.",
   "Emergency purge from the display button (or DI 6) overrides all other control: EMER ALM is set at BACnet priority 1, the damper opens fully for EMER TIMER, then flow holds at EXH STPT raised by EMER STPT until the button is pressed again.",
   "With a digital room unit (revision 26 and later), a command sent through the room unit puts the matching BACnet input Out Of Service.",
   "Loop gains, duct and sash dimensions, calibration and display settings are commissioning values; don't write them from the BMS routinely."
  ]
 },
